# algovault-bot.manifest — OPS-BOT-DEPLOY-PROVENANCE-W1
#
# THE declared set of repo paths that constitute a deploy of `algovault-bot`, read by BOTH
# ops/scripts/host-deploy.sh and ops/cron/bot-deploy-parity.sh. One list, two consumers — a
# deploy tool and a parity canary that disagree about what "deployed" means will manufacture
# phantom MISSING/ORPHAN findings forever.
#
# ── Why this file exists at all ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Before it, the deployed path set was AMBIENT: whatever pattern the last hand-rsync happened
# to use. Measured on the live host 2026-08-02: `audits/` and `hooks/` are tracked in the repo
# but ABSENT from /opt/algovault-bot, while `.github` and `.gitignore` ARE present. Nobody
# decided that. And an inferred set produces false findings on its very first run — during R0
# a parity check that compared `git ls-tree` (all files) against `find -name '*.py'` reported a
# MISSING that did not exist. A guard that cries wolf once gets ignored forever, so the set is
# DECLARED, with a reason on every line.
#
# Format: one entry per line, `<verb> <path>  # reason`.
#   deploy  — materialized from the commit and atomically swapped in
#   ignore  — present on the host but deliberately NOT deployed and NOT reported as ORPHAN
# Anything on the host that is neither is a genuine ORPHAN and is reported.

# ── deployed ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
deploy  src              # the package itself; ExecStart runs `-m algovault_bot.alert_engine`
deploy  scripts          # referral-notify-drain.sh is on a live root cron (14:25 et al)
deploy  tests            # present on the host today; keeping parity is a smaller change than
                         # deciding to strip them, which belongs to whoever wants the space
deploy  pyproject.toml   # `uv sync` reads it; a drifted copy silently mis-resolves deps
deploy  README.md        # harmless, already there, cheaper to keep than to argue about

# ── on the host, deliberately not deployed ──────────────────────────────────
ignore  .venv            # 5021 files / 171M of runtime, NOT in any commit. This is the entry
                         # that makes a whole-directory atomic swap unsafe: it would delete the
                         # interpreter the units execute (`/opt/algovault-bot/.venv/bin/python`)
ignore  .github          # CI config; no runtime role. Present as rsync residue
ignore  .gitignore       # same
ignore  .pytest_cache    # generated by running the suite on the host
ignore  src/algovault_bot.egg-info  # generated by an editable pip install during deploy;
                         # a real build artifact, surfaced as 6 ORPHANs by the canary's
                         # first live run. `ignore` matches inside deploy paths, not just
                         # at top level, so one list still governs both consumers
ignore  DEPLOYED_AT      # epoch stamp read by closedbar-w1-liveness.sh
ignore  DEPLOYED_SHA     # this wave's provenance stamp, written by host-deploy.sh
ignore  DEPLOYED_MANIFEST.sha256  # the per-file lockfile the parity canary verifies against
ignore  .pyproject.sha   # dep-sync fingerprint, so uv sync runs only when pyproject moved

# ── tracked in the repo but NOT deployed, by decision ───────────────────────
# audits/  — wave endpoint-truth records; documentation, never executed on the host
# hooks/   — git hooks; installed into a developer's checkout, meaningless on a server
